    "spanUnit": "codepoint",
    "text": "In July 1969, three men flew to the Moon, but only two of them walked on it. The third stayed in orbit, circling alone behind the far side, out of radio contact with every other human being. His name was Michael Collins.\n\nOver the next three and a half years, twelve men walked on the Moon. Neil Armstrong was the first and Gene Cernan was the last.\n\nSome historians call Collins the loneliest man in history. He wrote that he never felt that way.\n\nBehind those twelve were hundreds of thousands of engineers, technicians and seamstresses whose names almost nobody remembers."
  },
